<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<RecordType xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT and must stay that way. A comment
        placed ABOVE <RecordType> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the misleading
        error "unable to find matching parent xml file". The <description> below is deliberately
        short because RecordType.description is capped at 255 CHARACTERS - a cap this programme
        has now breached FIVE times, every one caught only by measuring.

        THE SELL-SIDE PSA. DPEG is the SELLER, so OUR legal issues the first draft and the
        counterparty is the BUYER. Parented by Disposition__c; Opportunity__c stays blank, and
        that blank is load-bearing - ContractExecutionService.handleExecution already drops any
        Contract Review with a null Opportunity__c, which is why the disposition PSA cannot
        create a phantom acquisition Transaction__c.

        ⚠ BOTH RECORD TYPES EXPOSE THE SAME FOUR Negotiation_Status__c VALUES, AND THAT IS THE
        POINT - IT IS NOT A COPY-PASTE THAT SOMEONE FORGOT TO SPECIALISE. Initial Draft ->
        Revised -> Ready for Execution -> Executed are ALREADY exactly the four states the
        client document names for the sell-side PSA. This is the one place in Tranche 3 where
        the two sides genuinely share a vocabulary: LOI__c needed five new stage values and
        NDA__c needed a whole second set, but the PSA needed none. The consequence is concrete -
        Contract_Review__c keeps ONE stage map in RecordStageAdvanceService and needs no
        record-type-aware branch, unlike LOI__c and NDA__c. Adding a disposition-only status
        here would silently drag that Apex change back into scope.

        WHAT THE TWO TYPES ACTUALLY DIFFER ON is exactly two things: the counterparty token in
        Ball_In_Court__c (Buyer here, Seller on Acquisition_PSA) and which parent lookup is
        populated. That is the whole delta.

        🔴 'Buyer' vs 'Seller' IS THE INVERSION THIS TYPE EXISTS TO FIX. On a sale DPEG *is* the
        seller, so Ball_In_Court__c = 'Seller' would name DPEG - the same party 'Us' already
        names - and the field would carry no information at all. 'Us' is side-neutral and is
        exposed on both types; only the counterparty token flips. 'Buyer' was ADDED to the
        master value set in this same change, never renamed from 'Seller': a rename is a removal
        plus an add, which triggers the standing picklist-removal sweep rule and forces a
        migration on live acquisition rows that are correctly 'Seller' today.
        ⚠ Record-type picklist restriction is UI-ONLY and is NOT enforced by Apex DML. This file
        stops a USER picking 'Seller' on a sale; it does not stop CODE writing it.
        PsaVersionService is the only writer and is the only place that can actually enforce it.

        EVERY PICKLIST ON THE OBJECT IS LISTED HERE, INCLUDING ONES THIS CHANGE DOES NOT ALTER.
        A record type file that OMITS a picklist silently drops ALL of that picklist's values
        for the type. Contract_Review__c has exactly THREE picklists: Ball_In_Court__c,
        Negotiation_Status__c and Stage__c. The fields/ directory was walked field by field to
        establish that, and the walk corrected the design document, which also named
        Asset_Type__c and Deal_Type__c - both are formula TEXT fields, not picklists.

        🔴 Stage__c IS A DERIVED FIELD. Contract_Review_Stage_Sync recomputes it from
        Negotiation_Status__c on every save, and a direct write to it COMMITS AND IS SILENTLY
        DISCARDED - measured org behaviour. It is listed here only so its values do not vanish
        from the type. The disposition PSA must drive Negotiation_Status__c, never Stage__c.
        ⚠ Its three stage labels (PSA Drafting / Review / Contract Execution) are buy-side
        wording that reads acceptably on a sale and are DELIBERATELY NOT relabelled: the sync
        flow maps Negotiation_Status__c onto these exact strings, so renaming them would break
        it for both types to improve wording for one.

        THE THREE isActive=false LEGACY Stage__c VALUES ARE DELIBERATELY OMITTED
        ('Contract Execution (Signed)', 'Contract Negotiation', 'Prepare'). An inactive value is
        unselectable org-wide, so listing it grants nothing, while naming a value the platform
        does not consider live risks the exact "picklist value does not exist" rejection that
        cost 3A a two-phase deploy. ⚠ NO IN-REPO PRECEDENT EXISTS EITHER WAY - a sweep of every
        recordType file found none that references a field carrying inactive values, so this is
        a DEPLOY GATE, not a settled pattern.

        NO URL-ENCODING IS NEEDED IN THIS FILE. Inside a RecordType a picklist fullName must be
        URL-encoded (repo precedent: Prepare%2FReview on LOI__c, Dead%2FPass in Opportunity's
        business processes). Every value listed here contains only letters and spaces - spaces
        are NOT encoded - so all fullNames are literal. The one value that would have needed it,
        'Contract Execution (Signed)', is inactive and omitted.

        NO <businessProcess> ELEMENT. That element applies to Opportunity, Case, Lead and
        Solution only.

        🔴 HANDOFF - APEX, NOT BUILT HERE. ContractExecutionService needs a record-type branch so
        an EXECUTED SALE moves Disposition__c.Disposition_Stage__c to 'Closing' instead of
        stamping an Opportunity. That is the behavioural half of this record type and without it
        Disposition_PSA is inert past Executed. It is developer work and was explicitly out of
        3C's declarative scope, as is the OpportunityReviewService:100 acquisition stamp
        (D16.3) documented in Acquisition_PSA's header.
    -->
    <fullName>Disposition_PSA</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>The sell-side PSA. DPEG is the seller, so our legal drafts first and the counterparty is the Buyer; Ball In Court reads Us / Buyer. Parented by Disposition; Opportunity stays blank. Same four Negotiation Status values as the acquisition type.</description>
    <label>Disposition PSA</label>
    <picklistValues>
        <picklist>Ball_In_Court__c</picklist>
        <values>
            <fullName>Us</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Buyer</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
    </picklistValues>
    <picklistValues>
        <picklist>Negotiation_Status__c</picklist>
        <values>
            <fullName>Initial Draft</fullName>
            <default>true</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Revised</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Ready for Execution</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Executed</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
    </picklistValues>
    <picklistValues>
        <picklist>Stage__c</picklist>
        <values>
            <fullName>PSA Drafting</fullName>
            <default>true</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Review</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Contract Execution</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
    </picklistValues>
</RecordType>
